From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium meta-browser maintainers <meta-browser@lists.openembedded.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v8: gate sanitizer features on sanitizer runtime builds

Chromium's release hardening enables trap-only sanitizer checks such as
array-bounds and return. Clang 20 does not support
-fsanitize-ignore-for-ubsan-feature, so these flags make __has_feature report
undefined_behavior_sanitizer in V8 even though no sanitizer runtime is linked.
That causes V8 to reference __sanitizer_set_death_callback at link time.

Pass the actual Chromium sanitizer-build state to V8 and only enable V8's
sanitizer-specific code when a sanitizer runtime is in use.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]
---
 v8/BUILD.gn          | 4 ++++
 v8/src/base/macros.h | 6 +++---
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v8/BUILD.gn b/v8/BUILD.gn
--- a/v8/BUILD.gn
+++ b/v8/BUILD.gn
@@ -905,2 +905,5 @@
 
+  if (using_sanitizer) {
+    defines = [ "V8_USE_SANITIZER" ]
+  }
 }

diff --git a/v8/src/base/macros.h b/v8/src/base/macros.h
--- a/v8/src/base/macros.h
+++ b/v8/src/base/macros.h
@@ -205,1 +205,1 @@
-#if defined(__has_feature)
+#if defined(V8_USE_SANITIZER) && defined(__has_feature)
@@ -219,1 +219,1 @@
-#if defined(__has_feature)
+#if defined(V8_USE_SANITIZER) && defined(__has_feature)
@@ -226,1 +226,1 @@
-#if defined(__has_feature)
+#if defined(V8_USE_SANITIZER) && defined(__has_feature)
